     "page": 2,
     "text": "OLLOW-UP PLAN:\nMs. Robinson was discharged home in stable condition. She was advised to follow up with her primary care physician within one week for a post-discharge evaluation. She will also continue regular follow-ups with her hepatologist for chronic hepatitis B management and her nephrologist for polycystic kidney disease. \n\nSOCIAL HISTORY:\nMs. Robinson reports consuming approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week. She denies tobacco use. \n\nDISCHARGE INSTRUCTIONS:\n- Continue all discharge medications as prescribed.\n- Maintain a healthy diet and regular exercise routine.\n- Avoid nephrotoxic agents and maintain adequate hydration.\n- Report any new or worsening symptoms immediately.\n\nFINAL DIAGNOSES:\n1. Polycystic kidney disease\n2. Chronic hepatitis B\n3. History of TIA\n4. Rosacea\n5. Cataracts\n6. Contraception\n\nThis discharge summary was prepared by Dr. David Melton, Family Medicine, Wright and Sons Clinic. \n\n[Signature]\nDr. David Melton\nFamily Medicine\nWright and Sons Clinic\n"
