     "text": "Ross Ltd Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Barbara Robinson in consultation on 13, 2024. This was a follow-up visit for her chronic hepatitis B, which is currently well controlled. \n\n**History:**\nBarbara was diagnosed with chronic hepatitis B on July 24, 2024. Since then, she has been compliant with her medications, which include tenofovir 300 mg and entecavir 0.5 mg daily. She reports no significant side effects from these medications. She has also been following a healthy diet and has been avoiding alcohol, though she does consume approximately 10 drinks per week. \n\n**Exam:**\nOn examination, Barbara appeared well with no signs of hepatic decompensation. Her blood pressure was 114/79, and her weight was 172 pounds. Her was soft, non-tender, and without hepatosplenomegaly. The rest of her physical examination was unremarkable.\n\n**Impression:**\nBarbara's chronic hepatitis B remains controlled with current therapy. Her liver function tests and viral load have been consistently within normal limits.\n\n**Recommendations:**\nContinue tenofovir 300 mg and entecavir 0.5 mg daily. Monitor liver function tests and viral load every three months. Encourage continued lifestyle modifications, including further reduction in alcohol intake if possible.\n\nThank you for referring Barbara for this consultation. Please do not hesitate to reach out if further information is needed.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Jonathan Smith \nGastroenterologist \nRoss Ltd Clinic\n"
